Package: datablinder
Title: Synthetic Look-Alike Copies of Sensitive Data Files
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Alex", "Gallinat", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "baloo.142@gmail.com")
Description: Replaces the contents of a sensitive or proprietary data file with
    synthetic values while keeping the columns, classes, formats and file type
    identical, so that analysis code written against the anonymised copy runs
    unchanged on the real data. Intended for sharing the structure of a dataset
    with a collaborator or with an AI assistant (a large language model or LLM
    chatbot) without sharing its contents. Reads and writes delimited text,
    'Excel', 'SPSS', 'Stata', 'RDS' and 'Parquet' files, and includes a local
    'Shiny' app and a command line script. Reduces disclosure risk; it offers
    no formal privacy guarantee.
